This is a telescoping series. We can rewrite the expression as $\sum_{j = 0}^\infty \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-j - k^2 - (k + j)^2}$. We can then factor out a $2^{-j}$ and rewrite the expression as $\sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-k^2 - (k + j)^2}$. We can then factor out a $2^{-k^2}$ and rewrite the expression as $\sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-k^2} 2^{-(k + j)^2 - k^2}$. We can then factor out a $2^{-k^2}$ and rewrite the expression as $\sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-k^2} 2^{-(k + j)^2 - k^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-k^2} 2^{-(k^2 + 2kj + j^2) - k^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-k^2} 2^{-2kj - j^2}$. We can then factor out a $2^{-2kj}$ and rewrite the expression as $\sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-k^2} 2^{-2kj} 2^{-j^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty 2^{-k^2} (2^{-j})^{2k} 2^{-j^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty (2^{-j})^{2k+1} 2^{-j^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty (2^{-j})^{2k+1} 2^{-j^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty (2^{-j})^{2k+1} 2^{-j^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} \sum_{k = 0}^\infty (2^{-j})^{2k+1} 2^{-j^2} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{-j} (2^{-j})^{j^2+1} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{- j(j+1) -j} = \sum_{j = 0}^\infty 2^{- j^2-j} = \frac{1}{2}\zeta(2) = \boxed{\frac{\pi^2}{12}}.
{/eq}
